-- title:
--   Blow-up chart surjects onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring
-- statement:
--   Throughout, write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A (↥K) j` for the $A$-subalgebra `chartAlg A (↥K) {j}` of $K$ attached to $j$, with `jChartFin A (↥K) j` the element $j$ regarded in $C$, and $\kappa :=$ `ResidueField A` for the residue field of $A$.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** A prime $q$ with $5 \le q$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero and an element $\xi \in L$ that is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` that some ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$.
--
--   **Function field.** An intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq$ `LaurentSeries L` with `hK` requiring $K$ to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the field generated over $L$ inside `LaurentSeries L` by the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational function field of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ attached to the subgroup `levelH (q*ℓ) M'`, the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell))^\times$.
--
--   **Base ring.** A discrete valuation ring $A$ which is a domain, Henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ a fraction field of $A$, and a compatible $A$-algebra structure on $K$ ($A \to L \to K$ a scalar tower); the hypotheses $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and that $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`). An element $j \in K$, nonzero, whose image in `LaurentSeries L` is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the coefficientwise transport to $L$ of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$. A uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A$ ($\mathfrak{m}_A = (\varpi)$) and an element $\varpi_t \in A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   **Supersingular point of the chart.** A maximal ideal $y \subseteq C$ containing the image of $\varpi$, and the hypothesis `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with $\ker \varphi = y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0 \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **Point of the two-chart model.** A point $z$ of the scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A (↥K) j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the two chart morphisms over $\operatorname{Spec} A$), an element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk at $z$ required by `hϖz` to be the germ at $z$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi$ through `toBase`, and `hz` asserting $\varpi_z \in \mathfrak{m}$ of that stalk; a point $y'$ of `XFin A (↥K) j = Spec C` with `ιFin` carrying $y'$ to $z$, the same supersingularity hypothesis `hss'` for homomorphisms out of $C$ with kernel $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, and `hy'y` : $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$.
--
--   **Local model at $z$.** A complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$ (a domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal), a ring homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, power series $f_1, u_1, v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1 - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the second term being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ with respect to its maximal ideal onto
--   $$S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v_1 - f_1u_1\big),$$
--   with `mkS` the quotient map.
--
--   **Blow-up chart.** An ideal $J \subseteq C$ and an $A$-subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ required by `hB` to be the scalar restriction to $A$ of the $C$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $\{x \in K : \exists\, i \in J,\ x\cdot \varpi_t = i\}$, that is $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$, together with `hCB` : $C \le B$.
--
--   Write $\Psi := e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} : C \to S$ for the composite of the germ homomorphism `germY` of $C$ into the stalk at $z$ (built from `ΓSpecIso`, the `appIso` of `ιFin` on the top open and the germ at $z$ of the open image of `ιFin`), the canonical map into the adic completion, and $e_1$. Put $\mathfrak{M} := (\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi), \mathrm{mkS}\,X_0, \mathrm{mkS}\,X_1) \subseteq S$ and $\mathfrak{N} := (\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t), \mathrm{mkS}\,X_0, \mathrm{mkS}\,X_1) \subseteq S$.
--
--   **Hypothesis `hbridge`** (nine clauses): $\Psi^{-1}\mathfrak{M} = y$; for every $n$ and every $s \in S$ there is $a \in C$ with $\Psi(a) - s \in \mathfrak{M}^n$; $\Psi$ agrees on the image of $A$ with $a \mapsto \mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1 a)$; every $c \in C$ is congruent modulo $y$ to the image of some $a \in A$; every $w \in W_1$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ to some $\sigma_1 a$; $\sigma_1^{-1}\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = \mathfrak{m}_A$; $\mathfrak{M}$ is maximal; every maximal ideal of $S$ equals $\mathfrak{M}$; and $S$ is flat as a $C$-module for the algebra structure given by $\Psi$.
--
--   **Hypothesis `hcentre`** (four clauses): $\Psi(J)S = \mathfrak{N}$; there is an ideal $I \subseteq C$ with $J = \Psi^{-1}\mathfrak{N} \cap I$ and $I + y = C$; $J \le y$; and the image of $\varpi_t$ in $C$ lies in $J$.
--
--   Finally, an algebra structure `inst` of the field `GaloisField q 2` (that is $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$) on $\kappa$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let $L_{\mathrm{loc}} :=$ `Localization.Away (mkS (C (σ₁ ϖt)))` with structure map $\iota_S : S \to L_{\mathrm{loc}}$, let
--   $$x_0 := \iota_S(\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0)\cdot \mathrm{invSelf}, \qquad x_1 := \iota_S(\mathrm{mkS}\,X_1)\cdot \mathrm{invSelf}$$
--   where `IsLocalization.Away.invSelf` is the inverse of $\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$ in $L_{\mathrm{loc}}$, and let $R_{\mathrm{loc}} \subseteq L_{\mathrm{loc}}$ be the subring generated by the range of $\iota_S$ together with $x_0, x_1$. Then there exist a ring homomorphism $\Phi : B \to L_{\mathrm{loc}}$, witnesses that $\iota_S(s) \in R_{\mathrm{loc}}$ for all $s \in S$, that $x_0, x_1 \in R_{\mathrm{loc}}$ and that $\Phi(b) \in R_{\mathrm{loc}}$ for all $b \in B$, a ring homomorphism $t_W : W_1 \to \kappa$, an element $c_R \in \kappa$, and ring homomorphisms $\rho_R : R_{\mathrm{loc}} \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) and $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the latter ring being `MvPolynomial (Fin 2) κ` modulo `drinfeldIdeal q κ`, with [`DrinfeldCurve.x q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L42) and [`DrinfeldCurve.y q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L44) the classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$), such that all of the following hold:
--
--   1. $\Phi$ extends $\Psi$ on the chart: for every $a \in C$, $\Phi$ of $a$ viewed in $B$ via `hCB` equals $\iota_S(\Psi(a))$.
--
--   2. $\Phi$ divides by $\varpi_t$ on the centre: for every $x \in B$ and every $i \in J \subseteq C$ with $x \cdot \varpi_t = i$ in $K$, one has $\Phi(x)\cdot \iota_S(\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)) = \iota_S(\Psi(i))$.
--
--   3. $t_W \circ \sigma_1$ is the residue map of $A$, and $t_W$ vanishes on $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$.
--
--   4. $c_R \neq 0$.
--
--   5. For every $F \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$, $\rho_R(\iota_S(\mathrm{mkS}\,F))$ is the image in `CoordRing q κ` of $t_W$ applied to the constant coefficient of $F$.
--
--   6. $\rho_R(x_0) = c_R\cdot$ [`DrinfeldCurve.x q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L42) and $\rho_R(x_1) = c_R\cdot$ [`DrinfeldCurve.y q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L44) (scalars via the structure map $\kappa \to$ `CoordRing q κ`).
--
--   7. $\rho(b) = \rho_R(\Phi(b))$ for every $b \in B$.
--
--   8. $\rho$ is surjective.
--
--   9. For $b \in B$, $\rho(b) = 0$ if and only if $b$ lies in the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $y$ under $C \to B$.
--
--   10. $\rho$ restricted to $A$ is the residue map of $A$ followed by $\kappa \to$ `CoordRing q κ`.
--
--   This identifies the fibre at the supersingular point $y$ of the blow-up chart $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$ of the integral model with the affine Drinfeld coordinate ring over the residue field of $A$, by transporting the question through the completed local blow-up chart at $z$: the quotient $B/yB$ is presented as [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) compatibly with the $A$-structure. It is used in the analysis of the Drinfeld fibre of the blow-up chart — the decomposition and inertia statements for level automorphisms, and the description of the adic completion of the blow-up chart in tangent coordinates.
